{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"84589aaa2d207f2d21adcc04e626bacfd86a128fe892b0853c29fcc40cbafc93","slug":"croaker","location":"/subrepos/demography/Croaker/Croaker.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"📖️ Assessing past and future life histories of an anadromous fish, the Atlantic croaker","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Daniel Grünbaum","given":"Daniel","family":"Grünbaum"},"name":"Daniel Grünbaum","affiliations":["School of Oceanography, University of Washington"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial Share Alike 4.0 International","CC":true}},"github":"https://github.com/organismal-systems/quant-org-bio","keywords":["models"],"copyright":"2026","affiliations":[{"id":"School of Oceanography, University of Washington","name":"School of Oceanography, University of Washington"}],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/organismal-systems/quant-org-bio/blob/main/subrepos/demography/Croaker/Croaker.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/organismal-systems/quant-org-bio/edit/main/subrepos/demography/Croaker/Croaker.md","thumbnail":"/build/5f1dc06f62355ac8c31ca00bce7d4ea7.jpeg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"Croaker.md","url":"/build/Croaker-b15e801b15bf04ad94a71fce74000f17.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The life history of marine organisms is under evolutionary selection in ways that are often difficult to quantify and understand.\nAn opportunity to advance our understanding arises when the evolutionary pressures change.\nThat is, the evolutionary response to a changing selective factor can tell us which direction that factor drives life history, and how strongly relative to other factors.","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"wFOKAv8Ylo"}],"key":"S5eWyJaGP4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We humans are providing ourselves with lots of opportunities to learn about life histories in this way.\nThis is particularly true with respect to mortality rates.\nMortality rates for pelagic species are usually very difficult to measure directly, and so their roles in life history evolution often remain somewhat speculative.\nHowever,  due to direct fishing pressure, and to indirect pressures such as by-catch and habitat degradation, humans have imposed major, and often quantifiable, increases in mortality rates in many species.\nIt would be surprising if these species did not evolve to have altered life histories under such dramatically changed conditions.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"qKJN6XoPNW"}],"key":"iXCIC0WXzk"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/5f1dc06f62355ac8c31ca00bce7d4ea7.jpeg","alt":"Wikipedia image of an Atlantic croaker","width":"600px","align":"center","key":"uc4hg6m1ay","urlSource":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Micropogonias_undulatus_RR_072120_0655_%2850142583921%29.jpg/960px-Micropogonias_undulatus_RR_072120_0655_%2850142583921%29.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"acroaker","identifier":"acroaker","html_id":"acroaker","enumerator":"1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"Unmn9WJt7w"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"P9GHRfu4Zb"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"EPLMKmfNmy"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"I3TCGEZxjk"},{"type":"text","value":"Wikipedia image of an Atlantic croaker.\nFor additional information on this species see this ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"eYrEPb28pj"},{"type":"link","url":"http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/huntwild/wild/species/croaker","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Texas Parks and Wildlife page","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"PWO2wHfZaH"}],"urlSource":"http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/huntwild/wild/species/croaker","key":"vN2HTFrvOS"},{"type":"text","value":")","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"B3G41g2lru"}],"key":"qVrK6rhdl4"}],"key":"joQKjvoEww"},{"type":"legend","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Citation :","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"qk75k66PCX"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Micropogonias undulatus","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"VIaSjKhzXj"}],"key":"kGpeY4yxq2"},{"type":"text","value":" RR 072120 0655 (50142583921).jpg, ","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"bXm6yUtR9w"},{"type":"link","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=File:Micropogonias_undulatus_RR_072120_0655_(50142583921).jpg&oldid=950950469","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://​commons​.wikimedia​.org​/w​/index​.php​?title​=​File:Micropogonias​_undulatus​_RR​_072120​_0655​_(50142583921)​.jpg​&​oldid​=​950950469","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"SI0flmUg35"}],"urlSource":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=File:Micropogonias_undulatus_RR_072120_0655_(5014258392